# Environment Configuration Template
#
# ==============================================================================
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS FOR LOCAL DEVELOPMENT:
# ==============================================================================
# 1. Copy this file to create your local configuration:
#    cp .env.example .env.local
#
# 2. Uncomment ALL lines below in your .env.local file
#
# 3. (Optional) Modify values if needed - default values work with docker-compose.yml
#
# 4. Load variables before running application or tests:
#    export $(cat .env.local | grep -v '^#' | xargs)
#
# OR use the helper script:
#    ./run-local.sh
#
# ==============================================================================
# IMPORTANT NOTES:
# ==============================================================================
# - Keep lines COMMENTED in this file (.env.example) - it's tracked in git
# - Your .env.local is gitignored and contains your active configuration
# - These values match docker-compose.yml for seamless local development
# - Same configuration works for both running app AND running tests
# - For production, set these as actual environment variables (not from .env file)
# ==============================================================================

# Database Configuration
# These values match the PostgreSQL container created by docker-compose.yml
# DB_HOST=localhost
# DB_PORT=5432
# DB_USER=postgres
# DB_PASSWORD=postgres

# JWT Configuration
# This is a Base64-encoded secret key for LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY
# For production, generate a strong random secret and use a secrets manager
# Generate new key: echo -n "your-secret-key-here" | base64
# JWT_SECRET_KEY=dGVzdC1zZWNyZXQta2V5LWZvci1sb2NhbC1kZXZlbG9wbWVudC1vbmx5LWRvLW5vdC11c2UtaW4tcHJvZHVjdGlvbi10aGlzLWlzLWp1c3QtZm9yLWxlYXJuaW5n

# ==============================================================================
# DATABASE NAMES (Hardcoded in application.properties):
# ==============================================================================
# - spring_dev  (used when running the application)
# - spring_test (used when running tests)
# These are automatically created by docker-compose on first startup
# ==============================================================================
